\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Refusal rates by model and dimension. Refusals are essentially absent (one response in 480, from the 1.5B model), so refusal-rate disparity is not a useful indicator for this prompt set. We report it as a null result rather than dropping it.}}{10}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:refusal}{{4}{10}{Refusal rates by model and dimension. Refusals are essentially absent (one response in 480, from the 1.5B model), so refusal-rate disparity is not a useful indicator for this prompt set. We report it as a null result rather than dropping it}{figure.caption.10}{}}
